# Morrowind Temple: Tuls Valen's "False Incarnate" (TT_FalseIncarnate). Elvil Vidron in Suran claims to be the
# Nerevarine ("False Incarnate": 10). Talked round at disposition 65 ("Yes. But you are not the one I envisioned." 2:
# 50), he repents; Tuls Valen rewards the mercy (100, three healing potions).
# "Show him the Moon-and-Star ring" (3) is not taken: its line writes TT_Compassion 55, not this journal.
# PositionCell and Position stand in for the travel; bribes, repeated until they land, raise Elvil. The AddItem of
# gold stands in for money the player earned on the way.
# Run: python -m tools.live.test_instance mwtest --cases <this folder> --fast --checkpoints --stop-on-fail --load mwtest_tt_compassion_done --timeout 3600
# See docs/commentary/headless_testing.md#quest-runs

case tt_falseincarnate_start
talk tuls valen
ask duties
ask False Incarnate
expect GetJournalIndex TT_FalseIncarnate == 10
bye
end

case tt_falseincarnate_elvil
run
player->AddItem Gold_001 1000
player->Position 53888 -50900 192 0
until 900 "elvil vidron"->GetDistance player < 600
wait 120
talk elvil vidron
persuade bribe100 until "elvil vidron"->GetDisposition >= 65
ask False Incarnate
choose 2
expect GetJournalIndex TT_FalseIncarnate == 50
end

case tt_falseincarnate_done
run
player->PositionCell 3637 3900 14723 0 "Ald-ruhn, Temple"
until 600 "tuls valen"->GetDistance player < 600
wait 120
talk tuls valen
ask False Incarnate
expect GetJournalIndex TT_FalseIncarnate == 100
bye
end
